 "meshSurgeryReason": "2026-10-11 lane B (standing mesh-surgery approval): the Meshy mesh welds the axe arm (upper arm, forearm, hand and axe haft) to the cape and flank below the armpit, so raising the arm for the DEF g12 overhead chop tore the cape out with it (arm aims +319 edges past 2x even at half amplitude, Hips<->LeftArm/ForeArm/Hand). limb_cut_surgery.py, boxed to Blender z<=0.98 so the shoulder stays welded, splits the bridge faces by majority and duplicates the shared vertices (arm copies drop the body bones, body originals drop the arm bones); every original vertex is byte-identical, same mesh at rest. Second cut arm_c2 (from arm_c1, limb_cut_surgery.py --mixed-from, box on the flank under the armpit x 0.18-0.5, z 0.5-0.98): the arm still hung onto the cape/flank fur through a strip of mixed-weight vertices; 20 more bridge faces split, originals byte-identical."
